        "explicacao": "This is the chart that organises everything: six cases × three genders × singular and plural. Read it by columns: each column (masculine, feminine, neuter, plural) has its own pattern. The golden rule of the accusative: if the noun is inanimate (a thing), the accusative equals the nominative in the masculine, the neuter and the plural; in the feminine, -а becomes -у. If it is animate (a person or an animal), the accusative equals the genitive in the masculine and in the plural. The prepositional always comes with a preposition (в, на, о, при) and in the plural it ends in -ах or -ях. Examples: стол (m), книга (f), окно (n).",
